        "slide": 7,
        "slideId": "s7",
        "speaker": "Dr. Nova",
        "text": "Active Recall Checkpoint 1! An autonomous mammography screening model undergoes an FDA regulatory audit. Engineers report it was trained on a Parquet file labeled v3. However, the auditor discovers that the file on the training cluster has a different SHA-256 hash than the archived compliance artifact bearing the same filename. What is the legal consequence and how must the pipeline be redesigned? Select your choice on the slide.",
