        "text": "In contrast, John Rawls's Maximin Distributive Justice evaluates a system strictly by the expected utility of its least-advantaged subgroup g. Furthermore, to operationalize Non-Maleficence against catastrophic tail events, we compute the Benefit-to-Risk Ratio BRR as expected benefit divided by expected cost plus gamma times the standard deviation of cost, where gamma quantifies downside risk aversion.",
